  "system": {
    "name": "Redis Iris Demos",
    "summary": "A local demo app that shows Redis Iris behind a chat agent, with one swappable domain pack per industry. A React chat UI streams each question to a FastAPI backend, which runs a fixed pipeline: a semantic-routing guardrail, a LangCache lookup, Agent Memory enrichment, then a LangGraph ReAct agent on OpenAI. The agent reads business data through Context Retriever MCP tools, which query the demo's Redis database. Setup scripts generate synthetic data for the active domain, create a Context Surface, load the data and seed memory and cache.",
    "highlights": [
      "All credentials sit in the local `.env` and are read by the backend and setup scripts; the browser holds none.",
      "`make setup` sends the Redis password to the Context Surfaces admin API, so Context Retriever reaches your database with it.",
      "At runtime the agent uses only the per-surface `MCP_AGENT_KEY`; `CTX_ADMIN_KEY` is used by setup scripts alone.",
      "One Redis database holds demo data, LangGraph checkpoints, router vectors and Agent Memory's `memory:*` keys; `flush_redis.py` wipes all but `memory:*`.",
      "Every prompt leaves the machine to OpenAI, LangCache and Agent Memory before the agent runs."
    ]
  },
